y-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:0b2d6544fc44a80acb0ce31ced55e769e6c75bd3c979259d4abcb922a9d49394","file":"preprints/The-Subcritical-Henon-Lane-Emden-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":58,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"ffe175cf15b69eda80fe1cbef2b544c1bc2c9060f9fc93d23dc1e5d502824dbd","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Subcritical-Henon-Lane-Emden-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:0b2d6544fc44a80acb0ce31ced55e769e6c75bd3c979259d4abcb922a9d49394","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Subcritical-Henon-Lane-Emden-Conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L58"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:lane-emden}\nFor every integer \\(n\\ge3\\) and \\(p,q>0\\) satisfying\n\\[\n \\frac{1}{p+1}+\\frac{1}{q+1}>\\frac{n-2}{n},\n\\]\nthere is no strictly positive \\(C^2(\\R^n)\\) solution of\n\\[\n -\\Delta u=v^p,\\qquad -\\Delta v=u^q\\qquad\\text{in }\\R^n.\n\\]"}
